at  they are explicitly stating is that the  rate of change that 5.4  in cpi over the last 12 months is the  rate at which inflation has changed in  these goods  that won't continue to be over 5 in the  future  well that essentially would mean that  inflation was compounding and so that we  would have to continue to grow at more  and more faster pace  in the future of course that's not going  to happen that's not how math happens  cars are not going to be  worth millions and millions of dollars  they only can go up so much  but what it doesn't  explain  is that the price increase  is not going away so while the rate of  change measured as inflation today  is not going to  continue to stay at inflated levels  the price increases that society is  experiencing  and the bottom 45 percent of americans  are getting hurt by are here to stay  chipotle  and other fast food restaurants are not  going to decrease their prices in the  future  those car prices that are going up are  unlikely to come down anytime soon  on top of that things like apparel or  other types of goods will continue to be  sold at elevated prices  part of that is because  you have increases in the labor market  if i go to an employee and i say hey i  am now going to pay you 15 an hour  next year i'm not going to come back to  you and say that i'll only pay you 13. i  have to pay you 15 or more into the  future and therefore if labor costs are  going up if the cost of my goods are  going up then i have to increase the  prices of what i sell to my consumer so  that i can pass those  cost increases on to the customer i am  not going to make less money as a  business simply because i have to pay my  employees more you as the end customer  are going to pay more  it is crazy to think  that people  actually want  to explain their prices are going to  come back down they're not going to the  rate of change is going to slow we are  not going to go from 5 to 10 to 15 to 20  over the next three four years because  